## Abstract

This high-school research project trains a ResNet-18 U-Net with an auxiliary benign-vs-malignant head on the BUSI breast ultrasound dataset, exports an INT8 ONNX model for fully in-browser inference, and reports honest internal and external metrics. On the held-out BUSI test set the **served INT8** model reaches Dice **{{INT8_DICE}}** (lesion-only **{{INT8_LESION_DICE}}**) and ROC-AUC **{{INT8_AUC}}**. External validation on BUS-BRA and BrEaST keeps segmentation closer to internal Dice (**{{BUSBRA_DICE}}** / **{{BREAST_DICE}}**) while classification AUC drops (**{{BUSBRA_AUC}}** / **{{BREAST_AUC}}**). Cleaning, leakage, caliper-inpainting, and TTA uncertainty experiments are included. Venue for this write-up: **site-only** (D5).

## Introduction

Breast ultrasound helps characterize masses, especially in dense breasts. Public datasets enable student projects but hide pitfalls: near-duplicate frames, burned-in calipers, and missing patient IDs. This project asks whether a small model can outline lesions in the browser — and how honest the scores remain under those pitfalls.

Related educational pages on the site cover BI-RADS context (a model score is not a BI-RADS category) and a surgeon's-view framing of size/margins (imaging size is not pathologic T-stage; model outlines are not surgical margins).

## Data

### BUSI (internal)

BUSI (Al-Dhabyani et al., *Data in Brief*, 2020) provides ~780 PNG ultrasound images labeled benign, malignant, or normal with masks. Multi-mask lesions are OR-merged. BUSI publishes **no patient IDs**; we group perceptual-hash near-duplicates so groups never cross splits. Annotation-flag rate (heuristic): **{{ANNOTATION_RATE}}** ({{N_FLAGGED}} / {{N_TOTAL}}).

### External (primary)

Per pre-registered protocol (`docs/EXTERNAL_VALIDATION_PROTOCOL.md`) and owner decision D1:

- **BUS-BRA** (Gómez-Flores et al., 2024; Zenodo CC BY 4.0): n={{BUSBRA_N}}, patients≈{{BUSBRA_NP}}
- **BrEaST** (Pawłowska et al., 2024; TCIA CC BY 4.0): n={{BREAST_N}}, patients={{BREAST_NP}}
- **BUS-UCLM**: skipped ({{BUSUCLM_SKIP}})

## Methods

- Architecture: ResNet-18 ImageNet encoder + slim U-Net decoder (160×160) with auxiliary classification head
- Training: grouped stratified splits; paired augmentations; checkpoint on lesion Dice; val-tuned seg threshold **{{SEG_THR}}**, min-component area **{{MIN_AREA}}**
- Served artifact: INT8 ONNX `models/v{{MODEL_VERSION}}/busi_unet.onnx` (sha256 {{MODEL_SHA8}}…)
- Browser: onnxruntime-web (WASM), Web Worker inference, same morphology post-process as Python eval
- Phase 2 extras: Telea caliper inpaint experiments, offline TTA uncertainty, Demo threshold sliders

