### Leakage ablation

Short schedule ({{LEAK_EPOCHS}} epochs × seeds {{LEAK_SEEDS}}), same grouped test: random vs grouped splits did not inflate validation Dice on this run (mean Δ val Dice random−grouped ≈ **{{LEAK_DELTA}}**). Residual leakage risk remains because patient IDs are absent. Source: `results/leakage_ablation.json`.

### Caliper / inpaint experiment

Flagged vs clean Dice gap on original test: flagged **{{EA_FLAGGED}}** vs clean **{{EA_CLEAN}}**. Erasing markers (E-a) did not collapse flagged Dice toward clean. Best E-c retrain seed did **not** replace served v1.0.0: external Dice failed the pre-registered swap rule (BUS-BRA {{EC_BUSBRA}} vs v1 {{BUSBRA_DICE}}; BrEaST {{EC_BREAST}} vs v1 {{BREAST_DICE}}). Source: `results/inpaint_experiment.json`.

### Uncertainty (TTA)

Spearman(ρ) between TTA disagreement and 1−Dice ≈ **{{UNCERT_RHO}}** on BUSI test (n={{UNCERT_N}}). Risk–coverage at 80% keep ≈ Dice **{{UNCERT_COV80}}**. Interpretation: agreement under flips — not a calibrated error probability. Source: `results/uncertainty.json`.

### Measurement agreement (BrEaST)

Model vs expert longest diameter (mm) Pearson proxy ≈ **{{MEAS_DIAM_R}}** (n={{MEAS_N}}); ≥20 mm threshold discordance ≈ **{{MEAS_T1T2}}**. Research only — not pathologic T-stage. Source: `results/measurement_agreement.json`.

## Limitations

- No patient IDs → residual near-duplicate / patient leakage risk
- Domain shift: classification AUC drops sharply on externals
- Calipers / HUD may still act as shortcuts
- 160² resolution loses fine detail; normal-image false positives ({{INT8_NFP}})
- Not clinically validated; no clinician review (D4 revoked)

